 "lines": {
  "arrival": [
   {
    "who": "Pell",
    "text": "Here we are. Tallowford."
   },
   {
    "who": "Pell",
    "text": "You can usually see it from the bend. Every window lit."
   },
   {
    "who": "Pell",
    "text": "Not one tonight. Not even old *Trim*'s, and he never lets his go out."
   },
   {
    "who": "Pell",
    "text": "His house is just up the road. I'll mind the raft."
   }
  ],
  "pell_idle_1": [
   {
    "who": "Pell",
    "text": "Trim's. Up the road. The house with all the lanterns."
   }
  ],
  "trim_grey": [
   {
    "who": "",
    "text": "Old Trim stands grey and still, one hand raised to a cold wick."
   }
  ],
  "verse_1_near": [
   {
    "who": "",
    "text": "A stone carved with verse. The letters have gone grey, as if they're thirsty."
   },
   {
    "who": "",
    "text": "Draw a circle round it: *Bloom*."
   }
  ],
  "verse_1": [
   {
    "who": "Verse-stone",
    "text": "I came here for the black inside your lamps,"
   },
   {
    "who": "Verse-stone",
    "text": "the soft soot a good wick leaves at dusk."
   },
   {
    "who": "Verse-stone",
    "text": "A light goes out; its dark stays gentle."
   },
   {
    "who": "Verse-stone",
    "text": "I thought that I could keep it so."
   },
   {
    "who": "",
    "text": "The last line glows like a wick. New glyph: *Kindle*. Open the brush and dab once, short and firm, on a wick."
   }
  ],
  "trim_wakes": [
   {
    "who": "Old Trim",
    "text": "Hm? Who let my lamp go out?"
   },
   {
    "who": "Old Trim",
    "text": "A paper fox. With a brush. Well. That's a first, and I've seen a few firsts."
   },
   {
    "who": "Old Trim",
    "text": "Something came down the river at dusk, black as a shut eye. Every lamp in the village went out at once."
   },
   {
    "who": "Old Trim",
    "text": "Funny. It put me in mind of a customer I had. An ink-maker, from upriver."
   },
   {
    "who": "Old Trim",
    "text": "He bought my *lamp-black*, the soot off the wicks. A jar a year, at first. Then a cartload."
   },
   {
    "who": "Old Trim",
    "text": "I asked what he wanted with so much dark. He said, 'Somewhere to keep the colours safe.' Never did follow him."
   },
   {
    "who": "Old Trim",
    "text": "Go and see *Marrow* at the dye yard, west of the square. If someone's shouting, it'll be her. If no one is, worry."
   }
  ],
  "trim_after": [
   {
    "who": "Old Trim",
    "text": "Dye yard. West. Follow the smell of wet wool."
   }
  ],
  "pell_idle_2": [
   {
    "who": "Pell",
    "text": "That's one lamp. Tallowford has a lot of lamps. You'd better get going."
   }
  ],
  "vats_near": [
   {
    "who": "",
    "text": "Black thorns have knotted themselves round the dye vats."
   }
  ],
  "marrow_grey": [
   {
    "who": "",
    "text": "Marrow stands grey to the elbows, her paddle lifted over a vat she can't reach."
   }
  ],
  "vats_cut": [
   {
    "who": "",
    "text": "The vats are free. The dyer's lamp is still cold."
   }
  ],
  "marrow_wakes": [
   {
    "who": "Marrow",
    "text": "And another thing! Oh. Where did everybody go?"
   },
   {
    "who": "Marrow",
    "text": "Look at my vats. Grey indigo. Do you know how hard it is to make indigo grey? Apparently not hard at all."
   },
   {
    "who": "Marrow",
    "text": "That's colour coming back round the lamp, isn't it? Then light them all, fox. Every one."
   },
   {
    "who": "Marrow",
    "text": "*Brindle*'s well is down the lane to the south-east. Can't dye without water. Can't do anything without water."
   }
  ],
  "marrow_after": [
   {
    "who": "Marrow",
    "text": "If you're done admiring my vats: Brindle. The well. Go."
   }
  ],
  "well_near": [
   {
    "who": "",
    "text": "Soot has packed the well to the brim, thick as fleece."
   }
  ],
  "brindle_grey": [
   {
    "who": "",
    "text": "Brindle stands grey in his doorway with an empty bucket, lips parted mid-count."
   }
  ],
  "well_cleared": [
   {
    "who": "",
    "text": "The soot blows off down the lane. Brindle's lamp still waits."
   }
  ],
  "brindle_wakes": [
   {
    "who": "Brindle",
    "text": "Forty-one. I was on forty-one buckets."
   },
   {
    "who": "Brindle",
    "text": "Then everything went quiet, and I've no idea where forty-two got to."
   },
   {
    "who": "Brindle",
    "text": "You've cleared the well! You've no idea how glad that makes me. Well. You have some idea. You did it."
   },
   {
    "who": "Brindle",
    "text": "Have you seen the little ones? *Flax* and *Pibbet*. They were playing under the *persimmon* in the square when it all went dark."
   }
  ],
  "brindle_after": [
   {
    "who": "Brindle",
    "text": "The square. The big bare tree. They'll be near it. They always are."
   }
  ],
  "tree_near": [
   {
    "who": "",
    "text": "The persimmon in the square stands bare. Not a leaf. Not one fruit."
   }
  ],
  "children_grey": [
   {
    "who": "",
    "text": "Two children stand grey by their door, halfway through a game of tag."
   }
  ],
  "tree_bloomed": [
   {
    "who": "",
    "text": "Leaves, then fruit, all at once, like a lamp turned up."
   }
  ],
  "children_wake": [
   {
    "who": "Flax",
    "text": "Pibbet, you're it, and no tagging back — oh."
   },
   {
    "who": "Pibbet",
    "text": "Fox."
   },
   {
    "who": "Flax",
    "text": "It's a paper fox, Pibbet. Don't poke it."
   },
   {
    "who": "Pibbet",
    "text": "Paper fox."
   },
   {
    "who": "Flax",
    "text": "Thank you for the tree. The fruit wasn't due till winter. You've done it early. That's allowed, I think."
   },
   {
    "who": "Flax",
    "text": "Are you lighting all of them? You have to do Aunt *Wherry*'s at the *ferry-house*, down by the jetty. She'll be cross if you skip her."
   },
   {
    "who": "Pibbet",
    "text": "Always cross."
   },
   {
    "who": "Flax",
    "text": "Nice cross."
   }
  ],
  "children_after": [
   {
    "who": "Flax",
    "text": "Ferry-house! East, by the river!"
   },
   {
    "who": "Pibbet",
    "text": "Persimmon."
   }
  ],
  "wherry_grey": [
   {
    "who": "",
    "text": "A woman in a river-grey coat stands in the ferry-house door, watching the water."
   }
  ],
  "ferry_lamp_lit": [
   {
    "who": "",
    "text": "The lamplight reaches across the river, and the river flinches."
   }
  ],
  "wherry_wakes": [
   {
    "who": "Aunt Wherry",
    "text": "Well. That's the second strangest thing I've seen on this jetty."
   },
   {
    "who": "Aunt Wherry",
    "text": "First was my nephew poling a raft upstream with his hat on backwards."
   },
   {
    "who": "Aunt Wherry",
    "text": "You're with Pell, then. Good. Somebody ought to be."
   },
   {
    "who": "Aunt Wherry",
    "text": "The ferry can't cross blind. The *ford-lamp*'s out on its post, up the north path, and something's hooded it."
   },
   {
    "who": "Aunt Wherry",
    "text": "Get that off and light it, and every lamp in Tallowford will remember what it's for."
   }
  ],
  "wherry_after": [
   {
    "who": "Aunt Wherry",
    "text": "North path. Tall post, out in the water. You can't miss it. Well. You could. Don't."
   }
  ],
  "verse_2_near": [
   {
    "who": "",
    "text": "Another stone of verse, grey as the first."
   }
  ],
  "verse_2": [
   {
    "who": "Verse-stone",
    "text": "Every colour, folded into one black:"
   },
   {
    "who": "Verse-stone",
    "text": "I ground it fine, and then I ground it finer."
   },
   {
    "who": "Verse-stone",
    "text": "The vat grew heavy as a held breath,"
   },
   {
    "who": "Verse-stone",
    "text": "and still I would not let it go."
   }
  ],
  "hood_near": [
   {
    "who": "",
    "text": "The ford-lamp wears a hood of soot, pulled down over its eyes."
   }
  ],
  "hood_off": [
   {
    "who": "",
    "text": "The hood tumbles into the river. High on the post, a wick waits."
   }
  ],
  "finale": [
   {
    "who": "Old Trim",
    "text": "There. Now that's a village."
   },
   {
    "who": "Marrow",
    "text": "Indigo! Proper indigo!"
   },
   {
    "who": "Brindle",
    "text": "Forty-two."
   },
   {
    "who": "Flax",
    "text": "Pibbet. Say thank you."
   },
   {
    "who": "Pibbet",
    "text": "Thank you, paper fox."
   },
   {
    "who": "Aunt Wherry",
    "text": "Ford's lit. Pell! Raft!"
   },
   {
    "who": "Pell",
    "text": "I saw. Whole river saw."
   },
   {
    "who": "Pell",
    "text": "Next stop's the *plain*. It's windy. Hold on to your ears."
   },
   {
    "who": "",
    "text": "A bead is added to Orimi's cord: *lamp gold*. The ink pot grows."
   }
  ],
  "pell_ready": [
   {
    "who": "Pell",
    "text": "Ready when you are. Hop on."
   }
  ],
  "trim_end": [
   {
    "who": "Old Trim",
    "text": "If you meet that ink-maker upriver, tell him I want my jars back."
   }
  ],
  "marrow_end": [
   {
